<title>INDIA: Good demand at Calcutta tea auction.</title>
<headline>Good demand at Calcutta tea auction.</headline>
<dateline>CALCUTTA, India 1996-09-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>All varieties attracted good demand at this week's Calcutta tea auction, traders said.</p>
<p>A total of 80,667 packages, including 6,131 packages of Darjeeling tea, were on offer.</p>
<p>Among CTC varieties, good liquoring Assam and Dooars were irregularly lower because of poor quality, trader said.</p>
<p>Among orthodox grades, clean whole leaf was two to three rupees easier while brokens and fannings were down by one to two.</p>
</text>
